Shuffle Joins:

Shuffle Join happens when spark needs to redistribute data across executors before performing join

Usecase:
If Both Dataframes are large

Shuffle Sort Merge Join:

Both sided sorted by join key

Default for large datasets

Shuffle hash Join:

Builds hash table after shuffle
Used when one side is moderately small

Performance Optimization for Shuffle join:

repartition on join key
df1 = df.repartition("id)

Handle data skew:
Use salting technique
Use skew join hints(Databricks feature)

Adjust Shuffle Parttions:

Tune it based on cluster size


